  "question": {
    "text": "The position of a moving car at time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math> is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>b</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mn>0</mn></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>and</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi></math>&nbsp;are real numbers greater than <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn></math>.&nbsp;Then the average speed of the car over the time interval <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> is attained at the point:",
